      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm trying to set up some reorder logic for our electronics parts. We're seeing some issues with lithium-ion battery cell stockouts when we hit peak season. Can you help me draft a formula or some basic rules for calculating safety stock levels, specifically considering lead times from our Shenzhen suppliers?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To calculate safety stock levels for lithium-ion battery cells, you can use the Continuous Review System (CRS) method. The basic formula is: Safety Stock = (Demand * Lead Time) / (Annual Demand * (1 - Demand-to-Inventory Ratio)). You'll need to input the following parameters: Annual Demand (how many cells you need to stock annually), Lead Time (ordinary time from supplier to your warehouse), and the Demand-to-Inventory Ratio (usually 2-15, depending on the product and business risk).",
