      "content": "Yes, you can categorize the types of disruptions and assign them varying severity levels. For example, you can create a disruption matrix with categories like:\n\n* Mild: Shipment delayed due to customs issues or paperwork errors\n* Moderate: Physical loss of shipment during transit\n* Severe: Supplier bankruptcy, closure, or complete logistics failure\n\nYou can then multiply the disruption's severity level by the lead time to get a weighted risk, which can be used in the safety stock calculation. This way, you can focus on the types of disruptions that have a disproportionate impact on your business, rather than just a general percentage risk.",
